# App page roadmaps — features only

Roadmap lanes on every App Project Page (`src/content/apps/<slug>.md` frontmatter, mirrored in `supply/apps/<slug>/app.md`) must describe **actual product features** the user experiences — nothing else.

## Keep

- User-facing features and capabilities (built, in progress, or genuinely planned).
- Short benefit-focused titles/descriptions in the visitor's language.

## Remove / never publish

- **User or owner tasks** (e.g. "Finish Play listing graphics", "First internal test upload", "review privacy copy").
- **Internal/engineering/release chores** (Console setup, CI, version bumps, refactors, QA).
- **"Not planned" / out-of-scope lanes** — do not list things you will not build; it implies they were considered.
- Task IDs, version numbers, or the word "shipped" on the public page.

## Example

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — internal task + not-planned lane
- id: now
  label: Before public release
  items:
    - title: Finish Google Play listing graphics and Console setup
- id: later
  label: Not planned
  items:
    - title: Dark mode

# ✅ GOOD — real upcoming feature
- id: next
  label: After release · Polish
  items:
    - title: Tap a heatmap cell for fact detail
      description: Attempts and last practised.
      status: planned
```

If a lane would only contain tasks/chores, omit the lane. Empty lanes are hidden at render (`src/lib/apps.ts`).
